            <ArticleTitle>Acute ischemic exacerbation of rheumatic mitral regurgitation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>928-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a patient who developed acute severe exacerbation of mild rheumatic mitral regurgitation caused by ischemia in the territory of a small, non-dominant circumflex coronary artery without myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
